<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Turk Shahis</h1><p class="st-meta">665 CE – 822 CE (approx.) · capital Kabul</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Turkic dynasty that ruled Kabul and Gandhara for over 150 years, blocking the Arab advance into the Indian subcontinent.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 665 a Turkic dynasty, probably linked to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/western-turkic-khaganate">Western Turkic Khaganate</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokharistan">Tokharistan</a>, replaced the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nezak-huns">Nezak Huns</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapisa">Kapisa</a>. Its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barha-tegin">Barha Tegin</a> claimed a long descent, and al-Biruni later recorded traditions of a line of sixty kings.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Turk Shahis ruled a largely Buddhist and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> population from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a>, and later also <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gandhara">Gandhara</a>, issuing coins with Bactrian and Brahmi legends. They received <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-tang">Tang</a> Chinese titles; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tegin-shah">Tegin Shah</a> was recognised in the 720s. Allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zunbils">Zunbils</a> to the south, they repeatedly fought off Arab armies from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khurasan</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the early 9th century the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mamun">al-Ma'mun</a> forced the last Turk Shahi king to submit and convert, and soon after, around 822, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kallar">Kallar</a> overthrew the dynasty, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hindu-shahis">Hindu Shahis</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 665 CE – 822 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central Asia and the Steppe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:72.94%;width:3.12%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>665 CE – 822 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kabul</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Barha Tegin, Tegin Shah, Lagaturman</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bactrian, Old Turkic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, <a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kabul Shahis (Turk), Turkic Shahis</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=744&amp;focus=turk-shahis" aria-label="Turk Shahis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6437 927 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Turk Shahis lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6757 1183L6134 1224"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6757 1183h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6757 1183h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kabul. <a href="/atlas?year=744&amp;focus=turk-shahis">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
